config BCM4775X_GNSS
	tristate "Broadcom BCM4775x GNSS receiver on SPI (lhd interface)"
	depends on SPI && GPIOLIB && REGULATOR
	help
	  The Broadcom BCM4775x GNSS receiver on SPI, as used in Google's
	  Pixel 7 phones. It exposes the chip's SSI link as /dev/ttyBCM and
	  the /dev/bbd_* nodes for Broadcom's own location daemons (lhd,
	  gpsd), which load the chip's patch and produce the positions.

	  To compile this driver as a module, choose M here: the module
	  will be called bcm4775x-gnss.
